      "original_record": "before",
      "value": "Let \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}].$\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $A$ is **not** invertible\n\nII. The lines $2x-3y=1$ and $2x-2y=2$ intersect at exactly one point\n\nIII. $Ax=0$ has no solution",
